<p data-start="1051" data-end="1177">But it takes a few more steps like installing <code data-start="1097" data-end="1107">gh-pages</code> and deploying from your project <span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center select-none relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid="webpage-citation-pill" style="width: 79px;"><a href="https://blog.logrocket.com/gh-pages-react-apps/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://blog.logrocket.com/gh-pages-react-apps/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" class="flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]! select-none" style="max-width: 79px;"><span class="relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between overflow-hidden" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">LogRocket Blog</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
<hr data-start="1179" data-end="1182">
<h2 data-section-id="bvneeq" data-start="1184" data-end="1214">🔥 What I recommend for you</h2>
<p data-start="1215" data-end="1276">Since you’re running a food truck:<br>
👉 <strong data-start="1253" data-end="1276">Netlify is the move</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1277" data-end="1343">
