 my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="c44078be-81ce-4e75-a426-e17355d19e6a" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="234" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">I’ll help you get past the Netlify error. Netlify now commonly shows <strong data-start="69" data-end="90">“Add new project”</strong> instead of “Add new site,” and the ZIP may be failing because Netlify’s drag-and-drop usually wants an <strong data-start="194" data-end="213">unzipped folder</strong>, not the ZIP itself.</p></div></div></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="0458dd6a-5c17-4de4-bba0-a9decf0a206f" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="271" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">The fix is: <strong data-start="12" data-end="47">don’t drag the ZIP into Netlify</strong>. Netlify’s manual drag-and-drop instructions say to drag a <strong data-start="107" data-end="152">project folder containing your site files</strong>, like an <code data-start="162" data-end="174">index.html</code> file, into Netlify Drop. I’ll give you a new package that you unzip first, then drag the folder.</p></div></div></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><button type="button" class="text-token-text-tertiary hover:text-token-text-primary dark:hover:text-token-text-primary flex items-center gap-0.5 text-start dark:text-(--interactive-label-tertiary-default)">Thought for 10s<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon-xs"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-430d4e28.svg#b140e7" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="a12c342f-afc4-4717-a652-847bf7349708" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5-thinking" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="108">Use this one: <span class="" data-state="closed"><button class="behavior-btn hover:entity-accent focus-visible:focus-ring entity-underline inline cursor-pointer appearance-none border-0 bg-transparent p-0 text-start align-baseline text-inherit" type="button">Download Netlify folder ZIP</button></span></p>
<p data-start="110" data-end="126">Do this exactly:</p>
<ol data-start="128" data-end="315">
<li data-section-id="z88sfx" data-start="128" data-end="143">
<p data-start="131" data-end="143">Download it.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="gwmw2a" data-start="144" data-end="160">
<p data-start="147" data-end="160"><strong data-start="147" data-end="160">Unzip it.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1r72iil" data-start="161" data-end="199">
<p data-start="164" data-end="199">Open Netlify → <strong data-start="179" data-end="198">Add new project</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="127ljt4" data-start="200" data-end="230">
<p data-start="203" data-end="230">Choose <strong data-start="210" data-end="229">Deploy manually</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="h1ykm0" data-start="231" data-end="315">
<p data-start="234" data-end="315">Drag the <strong data-start="243" data-end="262">unzipped folder</strong> named <code data-start="269" data-end="301">chef-daddy-rays-netlify-folder</code>, not the ZIP.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="317" data-end="457">Netlify says manual drag-and-drop should use a project folder containing site files like <code data-start="406" data-end="418">index.html</code>. <span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center select-none relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid="webpage-citation-pill" style="width: 81px;"><a href="https://docs.netlify.com/deploy/create-deploys/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://docs.netlify.com/deploy/create-deploys/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" class="flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]! select-none" style="max-width: 81px;"><span class="relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between overflow-hidden" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">docs.netlify.com</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>

