l agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="5ec8c5e1-45a0-4271-93da-967f71a001ab" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-3" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="109">Good question — this is where most people get stuck. I’ll keep it simple and tailored to what you’re doing 👇</p>
<hr data-start="111" data-end="114">
<h1 data-section-id="1n6rypw" data-start="116" data-end="150">🧠 First — understand your setup</h1>
<p data-start="151" data-end="217">Right now your site is a <strong data-start="176" data-end="196">static HTML site</strong> (not React anymore).</p>
<p data-start="219" data-end="233">👉 That means:</p>
<ul data-start="234" data-end="330">
<li data-section-id="1bmzkzm" data-start="234" data-end="262">
<p data-start="236" data-end="262">No “build” step needed ✅</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="fwbtgm" data-start="263" data-end="293">
<p data-start="265" data-end="293">No coding tools required ✅</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ersr65" data-start="294" data-end="330">
<p data-start="296" data-end="330">You edit it like a simple file ✅</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="332" data-end="335">
<h1 data-section-id="1w5vcjf" data-start="337" data-end="366">✏️ How to EDIT your website</h1>
<h2 data-section-id="ctg9xq" data-start="368" data-end="408">Option 1 (EASIEST – what I recommend)</h2>
<h3 data-section-id="1wjjhk6" data-start="409" data-end="437">Edit directly on Netlify</h3>
<ol data-start="439" data-end="627">
<li data-section-id="1tponv1" data-start="439" data-end="510">
<p data-start="442" data-end="510">Go to your site dashboard in <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Netlify</span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="16d4559" data-start="511" data-end="546">
<p data-start="514" data-end="546">Click <strong data-start="520" data-end="544">“Site configuration”</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="eezzbn" data-start="547" data-end="569">
<p data-start="550" data-end="569">Go to <strong data-start="556" data-end="567">Deploys</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1d51pyo" data-start="570" data-end="599">
<p data-start="573" data-end="599">Click your latest deploy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="h5vdei" data-start="600" data-end="627">
<p data-start="603" data-end="627">Click <strong data-start="609" data-end="627">“Browse files”</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="629" data-end="661">Now you’ll see your <code data-start="649" data-end="661">index.html</code></p>
<p data-start="663" data-end="699">👉 Click it → Edit → Save → Redeploy</p>
<hr data-start="701" data-end="704">
<h2 data-section-id="6bzspu" data-start="706" data-end="734">Option 2 (better control)</h2>
<h3 data-section-id="u4fevh" data-start="735" data-end="760">Edit on your computer</h3>
<ol data-start="762" data-end="911">
<li data-section-id="tgzzx0" data-start="762" data-end="789">
<p data-start="765" data-end="789">Right-click <code data-start="777" data-end="789">index.html</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="yvwc90" data-start="790" data-end="884">
<p data-start="793" data-end="803">Open with:</p>
<ul data-start="807" data-end="884">
<li data-section-id="13fro2b" data-start="807" data-end="828">
<p data-start="809" data-end="828">Notepad (Windows)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1pp9buq" data-start="832" data-end="884">
<p data-start="834" data-end="884">OR better: <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Visual Studio Code</span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1lb0u9g" data-start="886" data-end="911">
<p data-start="889" data-end="911">Change text like this:</p>
</li>
</ol>
