<p data-start="78" data-end="258">They changed the UI, so you <strong data-start="106" data-end="140">won’t see “Site configuration”</strong> unless you connected a Git repo. Since you used <strong data-start="189" data-end="206">manual upload</strong>, editing inside Netlify is basically not available.</p>
<hr data-start="260" data-end="263">
<h1 data-section-id="1owvak8" data-start="265" data-end="321">✅ Here’s the REAL way to update your site (your setup)</h1>
<h2 data-section-id="tysvx8" data-start="323" data-end="351">🔁 Every edit = re-upload</h2>
<p data-start="352" data-end="384">You edit locally, then redeploy.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1g04lgn" data-start="386" data-end="403">Step-by-step:</h3>
<ol data-start="404" data-end="561">
<li data-section-id="1m4iv0g" data-start="404" data-end="436">
<p data-start="407" data-end="436">Open your <strong data-start="417" data-end="436">unzipped folder</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="27arvb" data-start="437" data-end="464">
<p data-start="440" data-end="464">Right-click <code data-start="452" data-end="464">index.html</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="n26te7" data-start="465" data-end="561">
<p data-start="468" data-end="478">Open with:</p>
<ul data-start="482" data-end="561">
<li data-section-id="1n3uuo2" data-start="482" data-end="502">
<p data-start="484" data-end="502">Notepad (simple)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="13lqkyh" data-start="506" data-end="561">
<p data-start="508" data-end="561">or <strong data-start="511" data-end="561"><span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Visual Studio Code</span></span> (better)</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="563" data-end="566">
<h2 data-section-id="8uqoci" data-start="568" data-end="587">✏️ Example edits</h2>
