<p data-start="46" data-end="187">👉 When Windows only shows <strong data-start="73" data-end="105">“Compress” and NOT “Extract”</strong>, that means:<br>
<strong data-start="119" data-end="187">the file you downloaded is NOT a zip — it’s already just a file.</strong></p>
<p data-start="189" data-end="249">So what you actually need is a <strong data-start="220" data-end="248">folder you make yourself</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="251" data-end="254">
