>ChatGPT said:</h4><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="dbbd0459-664a-4fb6-9a6f-e82d4a565d47" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-3" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="65">Ahhh — NOW I see the real issue. You’re not doing anything wrong.</p>
<p data-start="67" data-end="213">👉 Your browser/device is <strong data-start="93" data-end="141">auto-extracting the ZIP when you download it</strong>, which is why you’re seeing <strong data-start="170" data-end="212">multiple files instead of one ZIP file</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="215" data-end="297">So Netlify is getting confused because you’re not uploading it the way it expects.</p>
<hr data-start="299" data-end="302">
<h1 data-section-id="6phtdr" data-start="304" data-end="336">🔥 SIMPLE FIX (THIS WILL WORK)</h1>
<h2 data-section-id="14e7qsb" data-start="338" data-end="366">✅ Instead of downloading…</h2>
<p data-start="368" data-end="423">👉 <strong data-start="371" data-end="404">Right-click the download link</strong> (don’t left click)</p>
<p data-start="425" data-end="459">Then click:<br>
👉 <strong data-start="440" data-end="459">“Save link as…”</strong></p>
<p data-start="461" data-end="510">This forces it to download as a <strong data-start="493" data-end="510">real ZIP file</strong></p>
<hr data-start="512" data-end="515">
<h1 data-section-id="1pmjhdt" data-start="517" data-end="534">🚀 THEN DO THIS</h1>
<ol data-start="536" data-end="641">
<li data-section-id="1tq05bg" data-start="536" data-end="554">
<p data-start="539" data-end="554">Go to Netlify</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1d9a5t5" data-start="555" data-end="603">
<p data-start="558" data-end="603">Click <strong data-start="564" data-end="601">Add new project → Deploy manually</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1mto52i" data-start="604" data-end="641">
<p data-start="607" data-end="641">Drag the ZIP file you just saved</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="643" data-end="646">
<h1 data-section-id="2koteo" data-start="648" data-end="674">🧠 Why this is happening</h1>
<p data-start="676" data-end="729">Some browsers (especially Edge/Chrome settings) will:</p>
<ul data-start="730" data-end="796">
<li data-section-id="1b1u4fp" data-start="730" data-end="752">
<p data-start="732" data-end="752">Auto-unzip downloads</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ftizzx" data-start="753" data-end="796">
<p data-start="755" data-end="796">Show you the contents instead of the file</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="798" data-end="863">That’s why you’re seeing:<br>
👉 multiple files instead of one <code data-start="857" data-end="863">.zip</code></p>
<hr data-start="865" data-end="868">
<h1 data-section-id="1ik6teh" data-start="870" data-end="918">🔁 Backup method (if right-click doesn’t work)</h1>
<p data-start="920" data-end="936">Do this instead:</p>
<ol data-start="938" data-end="1061">
<li data-section-id="12hr1zr" data-start="938" data-end="969">
<p data-start="941" data-end="969">Download the file normally</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1bnie5o" data-start="970" data-end="1003">
<p data-start="973" data-end="1003">Select all the files you see</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1uexm5a" data-start="1004" data-end="1061">
<p data-start="1007" data-end="1061">Right-click → <strong data-start="1021" data-end="1061">Send to → Compressed (zipped) folder</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1063" data-end="1091">Now you’ll have your own ZIP</p>
<p data-start="1093" data-end="1118">👉 Upload THAT to Netlify</p>
<hr data-start="1120" data-end="1123">
