<p data-start="76" data-end="232">Your computer/browser is <strong data-start="101" data-end="155">auto-extracting the zip immediately after download</strong>, which is why you’re seeing <strong data-start="184" data-end="231">separate files instead of one zipped folder</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="234" data-end="320">So the ZIP I’m giving you <strong data-start="260" data-end="274">is correct</strong>, but your system is opening it automatically.</p>
<hr data-start="322" data-end="325">
<h1 data-section-id="1katx7q" data-start="327" data-end="356">✅ WHAT YOU NEED TO DO (FIX)</h1>
<h2 data-section-id="15a47yx" data-start="358" data-end="395">🟢 Option 1 (FASTEST — works 100%)</h2>
<p data-start="397" data-end="416">After you download:</p>
<ol data-start="418" data-end="593">
<li data-section-id="1f8g3rz" data-start="418" data-end="445">
<p data-start="421" data-end="445">Go to your <strong data-start="432" data-end="445">Downloads</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="161m236" data-start="446" data-end="488">
<p data-start="449" data-end="488">You’ll see the files already “unzipped”</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1oz8w3x" data-start="489" data-end="524">
<p data-start="492" data-end="524">Select <strong data-start="499" data-end="524">ALL the files you see</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="xf1dzw" data-start="525" data-end="539">
<p data-start="528" data-end="539">Right-click</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="10nqkpv" data-start="540" data-end="593">
<p data-start="543" data-end="593">Click:<br>
👉 <strong data-start="553" data-end="593">Send to → Compressed (zipped) folder</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="595" data-end="610">Now you’ll get:</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="611" data-end="642"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-430d4e28.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼs ͼ16"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>chef-daddy-rays.zip</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="644" data-end="679">👉 THAT is your working upload file</p>
<hr data-start="681" data-end="684">
<h2 data-section-id="h32x9k" data-start="686" data-end="718">🟢 Option 2 (stop auto-unzip)</h2>
<p data-start="720" data-end="763">If you want it to download as ONE zip file:</p>
<h3 data-section-id="sg90aq" data-start="765" data-end="780">On Windows:</h3>
<ul data-start="781" data-end="827">
<li data-section-id="15rkllq" data-start="781" data-end="827">
<p data-start="783" data-end="827">Right-click download link → <strong data-start="811" data-end="827">Save link as</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="1y7ovaq" data-start="829" data-end="840">On Mac:</h3>
<ul data-start="841" data-end="913">
<li data-section-id="11t6el2" data-start="841" data-end="913">
<p data-start="843" data-end="913">Safari → Preferences → uncheck:<br>
👉 “Open safe files after downloading”</p>
</li>
</ul>
